# Pinned from the real red run of 2026-07-29 with the injection applied.
#
# WHY THIS RED AND NOT THE CONTENTION FAILURE ITSELF
#
# The defect's runtime symptom is `tmux new-session failed (exit 1): server
# exited unexpectedly`, and it WAS reproduced before the fix — 11 hits in 120
# rounds of the shared-server handoff race (a tmux server exits when its last
# session goes away, its socket outlives that decision by a moment, and the next
# client to arrive in that window is told the server vanished). The same 120
# rounds against a server the run owns and holds open produced 0.
#
# That signature is real but probabilistic — ~9% of rounds, load-dependent, and
# 0/250 on an idle machine. A proof that flakes is not a proof. So this artifact
# pins the deterministic half the task body asks for: the assertion that the
# spawned tmux command line carries no `-L`. It is the *cause*, one layer above
# the symptom, and it fails the same way on every host and every run.
#
# The behavioural half lives in the suite as
# `tmux_sessions_land_on_a_server_the_test_run_owns`, which asserts a real
# session is reachable on the owned server and NOT on the shared one. It is
# deliberately NOT in `cmd`: under the injection it would create its sessions on
# whichever server the environment selects — possibly the operator's own — and
# a proof must not damage what it proves.

